          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: A motorist observed a yellow light moving in the sky twice on September 21, 2009. The questionnaire for this observation, received by GEIPAN in February 2011, was not very detailed (very brief phenomena, night driving, observation through the window of a moving vehicle, very low altitude near the road) and lacks supporting evidence (such as a police report or pre-investigation), making it impossible to draw conclusions (it could be a reflection from vehicle headlights, a streetlamp, etc.). This testimony is inconsistent and lacks any strange characteristics. The unexplained case is classified C due to lack of information and an impossible investigation.",
